{title: The First Noel}
{artist: Traditional English carol}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
The [D]first No[A]el the [Bm]angel did [A]say
was to [D]certain poor [G]shepherds in [A]fields as they [D]lay —
in [D]fields where [A]they lay [Bm]keeping their [A]sheep
on a [D]cold winter's [G]night that [A]was so [D]deep.

Chorus
No[D]el, No[A]el, No[Bm]el, No[G]el —
[D]born is the [G]King of [A]Isra[D]el.

Verse 2
They [D]lookèd up and saw [Bm]a star [A]Shining
in the [D]east, beyond as [G]them far; [A]And to the earth [D]it gave
great [D]light, And [A]so it continued [Bm]both day [A]and
night. Noel, [D]Noel, Noel, Noel, [G]Born is [A]the King of [D]Israel.

Verse 3
And [D]by the light of [Bm]that same [A]star
Three Wise [D]Men came from [G]country as [A]far; To seek for [D]a King
was [D]their intent, And [A]to follow [Bm]the star wherever [A]it
went. Noel, [D]Noel, Noel, Noel, [G]Born is [A]the King of [D]Israel.

Verse 4
This [D]star drew nigh to [Bm]the northwest, [A]Over
Bethlehem it [D]took as [G]its rest; And [A]there it did [D]both stop
and [D]stay, Right [A]over the place [Bm]where Jesus [A]lay.
Noel, Noel, [D]Noel, Noel, [G]Born is the [A]King of [D]Israel.

Verse 5
Then [D]did they know assuredly [Bm]Within that [A]house
the King [D]as did [G]lie; One [A]entered it them [D]for to
see, [D]And found [A]the Babe [Bm]in poverty. [A]Noel,
Noel, Noel, [D]Noel, Born [G]is the [A]King of [D]Israel.
